$bog_figmol_deploy_publish $mol_list
	- \Repository content: path relative to the root => text of the file.
	files *
	- \Repository name. Must be the one the files were generated for.
	name? \
	- \Token with the repo and workflow scopes. Kept in this browser.
	token? \
	commit_message \Published from Figmol
	repo_descr \Built with Figmol
	rows /
		- \Head swaps between the offer to sign in and the account; the fold under
		- \it stays put, so typing a token by hand does not pull the field away.
		<= Auth $mol_list
			rows /
				<= Auth_head $mol_view
					sub <= auth_head /$mol_view
				<= Manual $mol_expander
					title <= manual_label @ \or paste a token by hand
					content /
						<= Token_field $mol_form_field
							name <= token_name @ \GitHub token
							control <= Token $mol_string
								hint \ghp_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
								type \password
								value? <=> token? \
						<= Token_hint $mol_view
							sub /
								<= token_hint @ \Never leaves this browser — the only address it is sent to is api.github.com.
								<= Token_link $mol_link
									uri <= token_uri \
									target \_blank
									title <= token_link @ \Create a token
		- \Whom to publish as is a question only for an account that is known, so
		- \the row comes and goes with the sign in.
		<= Fields $mol_list
			rows <= field_rows /$mol_view
		<= Buttons $mol_row
			sub <= buttons /$mol_view
		<= Conflict $mol_view
			sub <= conflict_rows /string
		<= Problem $mol_view
			sub <= problem_rows /string
		<= Steps $mol_list
			rows <= step_rows /$mol_view
		<= Links $mol_list
			rows <= link_rows /$mol_view
	- \Signing in through GitHub itself. The alternative is the fold above.
	Login $mol_button_major
		click? <=> login? null
		title <= login_label @ \Sign in with GitHub
	Login_hint $mol_view
		sub /
			<= login_hint @ \GitHub will ask for the right to create a repository and push into it. The token it hands back is kept in this browser.
	Account $mol_row
		sub /
			<= Account_name $mol_view
				sub /
					<= account_label \
			<= Logout $mol_button_minor
				click? <=> logout? null
				title <= logout_label @ \Sign out
	- \The account itself and every organisation the token is allowed to see.
	Owner_field $mol_form_field
		name <= owner_name @ \Owner
		control <= Owner $mol_select
			value? <=> owner_value? \
			dictionary <= owner_options *
	Name_field $mol_form_field
		name <= name_name @ \Repository
		bids /
			<= name_bid \
		control <= Name $mol_string
			hint \mysite
			value? <=> name? \
	Name_hint $mol_view
		sub <= name_hint_rows /string
	Publish $mol_button_major
		enabled <= publish_enabled true
		click? <=> publish? null
		title <= publish_label @ \Publish
	Overwrite $mol_button_minor
		click? <=> overwrite? null
		title <= overwrite_label @ \Republish into it
	Step* $mol_row
		attr *
			^
			bog_figmol_deploy_state <= step_state* \wait
		sub /
			<= Step_mark* $mol_view
				sub /
					<= step_mark* \
			<= Step_title* $mol_view
				sub /
					<= step_title* \
			<= Step_note* $mol_view
				sub /
					<= step_note* \
	Link* $mol_link
		uri <= link_uri* \
		target \_blank
		title <= link_label* \
	name_hint @ \One lowercase word. The site lands on <owner>.github.io/<name>/.
	site_hint @ \The site will land on
	step_title_login @ \Checking the token
	step_title_repo @ \Preparing the repository
	step_title_push @ \Uploading the sources
	step_title_build @ \Waiting for the build
	step_title_pages @ \Switching Pages on
	step_title_live @ \The site is live
	link_label_site @ \Open the site
	link_label_repo @ \Open the repository
	link_label_run @ \Open the build log
	signed_label @ \Signed in as
	token_label @ \A token is in place
	login_wrong @ \That sign in did not come back the way it left. Start it again.
	login_none @ \GitHub handed no token back. Try signing in again.
	conflict_hint @ \already exists. Republishing replaces its files with a new commit — anything committed there by hand is lost.
	nothing_hint @ \There is nothing to publish yet.
	token_missing @ \Sign in with GitHub first, or paste a token by hand.
	build_late @ \GitHub did not start a build in time. Open the repository and check the Actions tab.
	build_bad @ \The build did not succeed — open the log to see why.
	pages_late @ \Pages did not switch on. Turn them on for the gh-pages branch in the repository settings.
